# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Contact form delivery — EmailJS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Messages from /contact are sent with EmailJS and land in the inbox the
# EmailJS service is wired to (solutions@bitsbayltd.com).
#
# These three values are PUBLIC identifiers. EmailJS intends the Public Key to
# be visible in client-side code — it is origin-restricted and rate-limited on
# their side. They are already baked into src/lib/contact.js as defaults, so
# the form works without this file; set them here only to point a build at a
# different EmailJS account or template.
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=service_wfyb3vi
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=template_4feqe3k
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=o1sGgvXOrjeloB-wp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE ON THE EMAILJS PRIVATE KEY
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Your EmailJS account also has a Private Key. It is a SECRET and must never be
# added here or anywhere under src/ — anything Vite exposes with a VITE_ prefix
# is compiled into the public JavaScript bundle that every visitor downloads.
#
# The Private Key is only for server-to-server calls to the EmailJS REST API.
# If you later add a backend, keep it in a server-only variable (no VITE_
# prefix) so it never reaches the browser.
